node_modules/
dist/
# vendor/ is entirely generated: scripts/prepack.js copies host/, client/ and
# protocol/ in, and scripts/ffmpeg/build.sh drops the bundled ffmpeg binaries into
# vendor/ffmpeg/. Nothing in here is source.
#
# The ffmpeg binaries are ~17MB across four platforms and are rebuilt only when the
# pinned ffmpeg version changes, so keeping them out of history costs a rebuild per
# VERSION rather than per release. What that risks is packaging an installer with no
# binary in it, silently restoring the bug the bundling exists to fix - so the build
# scripts REFUSE to package without them. Provenance and the LGPL requirement are
# recorded in scripts/ffmpeg/README.md, which is tracked.
vendor/
